.TH AEGIS-CLI 1 "2026-11-04" "AIDriven NetDefense" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aegis-cli \- read-only loopback client for the AIDriven NetDefense daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aegis-cli
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aegis-cli
talks to the daemon over its loopback HTTP API and prints status, health, alerts and
analysis results. It never executes a response action, never reads the event store
directly and never prints the bearer token.
.PP
The daemon listens on a loopback address only, so the client must run on the same host.
The token is read from
.I /var/lib/aidriven-netdefense/secrets/api-token
which the package generates at install time; the client process must be able to read
that file, either as root or as a member of the
.I aegis
group.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aidriven-netdefense/aegis.conf.json
Daemon configuration. A conffile: edits survive upgrades.
.TP
.I /var/lib/aidriven-netdefense
Writable state: event store, checkpoint, analysis attempts, API token.
.TP
.I /opt/aidriven-netdefense/app
Installed payload, including the bundled Node.js runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
.BR "systemctl status aidriven-netdefense-daemon"
.PP
.BR "journalctl -u aidriven-netdefense-daemon"
.SH AUTHOR
PT-dove
